h the stub launcher records every claude invocation and calls() is used for deterministic counting elsewhere in this file, so the proof is host-speed dependent; the assertion belongs on the counted session-list reads, not on elapsed time.","why":"tests/suite/router.rs:5999-6005 asserts the 15s bound, but no deterministic substitute exists: tests/suite/router.rs:611 records only claude invocations in $STUB_STATE/calls and tests/suite/router.rs:784 calls() reads just that log, while scripts/router-worker.sh:661 invokes claude agents --json exactly once in both the one-pass fix and the quadratic predecessor (4fd99500:scripts/router-worker.sh prune block: one agents call, then a per-session cleanup over every run dir), so a count of session-list reads is 1 in both versions and would not guard the fix; a /tmp replica of the 120-dir setup took 0.59-2.09s on the fixed prune vs 25.5s for the old quadratic loop, so the 15s bound is calibrated to catch the regression (and the suite already uses such bounds at tests/suite/router.rs:112 and :573), leaving no host-speed flake risk and no observable drift."}],"nits":[{"location":"scripts/router-worker.sh:706","finding":"spawn ... --role \"\" matches the empty-string case arm and starts the worker at worker_default_effort instead of refusing with 'role must be worker|planner', while an empty --effort and an empty --permission-mode are both refused by the checks added for those.","waived":"the review is read-only and the run FAILs on four importants; the fix round may add the empty-role refusal in the same case arm under the fix-PASS that follows, and nothing observable changes meanwhile - the router's Bash guard cannot express an empty word, and the documented meaning of an omitted role is the worker's default level (skills/keel-router/references/worker-ops.md:106-109)"}],"fleet":{"dimensions":["correctness","efficiency","altitude"],"finders":3,"verifiers":6,"verifier_model":"deepseek-official/deepseek-flash","candidates":{"blocke